Subject: P5 Graph Procedure State Envelope And Checkpoint Nonauthority Contract V1
Date: 2026-05-27
Contract UUID: 9f963c2a-5fe4-4b65-9608-8617ca9f40c9

@ [p5_slice_surface] docs/slices/P5_LangGraph_Procedure_Runtime_Final_Slices.v1.sop
@ [p5_s01_output] docs/runtime/P5_Boundary_Import_And_Runtime_Obligation_Inventory.v1.sop
@ [p5_s01_review] docs/reviews/P5_S01_Completion_Review.v1.sop
@ [p8_proof_ledger_contract] docs/planning/P8_Proof_Ledger_And_Evaluation_Acceptance_Contract.v1.sop

& [P5GraphProcedureStateEnvelopeAndCheckpointNonauthorityContractV1] is the P5-S02 graph procedure state envelope and checkpoint nonauthority contract
  + [slice_id] is P5-S02
  + [slice_name] is graph procedure state envelope and checkpoint nonauthority contract
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_depth] is deeper_reasoning_required
  + [model_route_reason] is graph checkpoint state can preserve execution continuity but cannot become semantic authority or proof authority
  + [contract_result] is graph_state_and_checkpoint_nonauthority_defined_without_runtime_implementation
  + [next_gate_result] is P5-S03 may open
  + [dependency_installation_authorized] is false
  + [package_metadata_mutation_authorized] is false
  + [implementation_code_authorized] is false
  + [adapter_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [graph_runtime_execution_authorized] is false
  + [assignment_authorized] is false
  + [dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: define graph state and checkpoint records as contracts only
  = must: keep checkpoint records separate from SOP source authority, canonical specifications, proof ledgers, generated outputs, surface projections, assignment, dispatch, operations control, and live machine control
  = must: require SOP-first reconsideration when checkpoint resume semantics conflict with current source authority or proof ledger authority

& [P5GraphProcedureStateRequiredFieldSet] is the required field set for future graph procedure state records
  + [required_field] is graph_run_id
  + [required_field] is graph_run_uuid
  + [required_field] is procedure_id
  + [required_field] is procedure_uuid
  + [required_field] is graph_contract_ref
  + [required_field] is graph_contract_sha256
  + [required_field] is source_authority_ref_set
  + [required_field] is source_authority_sha256_set
  + [required_field] is kernel_record_ref_set
  + [required_field] is operator_contract_ref_set
  + [required_field] is proof_ledger_ref_set
  + [required_field] is checkpoint_ref
  + [required_field] is checkpoint_sha256
  + [required_field] is current_node_id
  + [required_field] is current_node_kind
  + [required_field] is pending_edge_set
  + [required_field] is pending_interrupt_ref
  + [required_field] is result_state
  + [required_field] is stale_trigger_set
  + [required_field] is nonpromotion_notice
  + [required_field] is no_dispatch_review
  + [required_field] is no_live_effect_review
  + [required_field] is resume_policy
  + [required_field] is downstream_consumption_gate

  = must: reject graph procedure state records that omit source authority, checkpoint identity, result state, nonpromotion notice, no-dispatch review, no-live-effect review, or resume policy
  = must: treat graph_run_id as a local natural key and graph_run_uuid as durable cross-surface runtime identity

& [P5CheckpointNonauthorityRules] is the checkpoint nonauthority rule set
  + [rule] is checkpoint state may preserve runtime continuity
  + [rule] is checkpoint state may support resume only when source authority and proof ledger freshness checks pass
  + [rule] is checkpoint state must not replace SOP source, canonical specifications, proof ledgers, or completion reviews
  + [rule] is checkpoint state must not promote generated outputs to source authority
  + [rule] is checkpoint state must not authorize assignment, dispatch, operations control, live machine control, dependency installation, package metadata mutation, or adapter implementation
  + [rule] is checkpoint state must carry stale triggers when any source authority, operator contract, proof ledger, path policy, nonpromotion policy, or no-live-effect boundary changes

  = must: render checkpoint nonauthority notices in downstream surfaces
  = must: route checkpoint authority conflict to SOP interrupt rather than continuing graph execution

& [P5CheckpointFreshnessAndResumeContract] is the checkpoint freshness and resume contract
  + [freshness_check] is source_authority_hash_match
  + [freshness_check] is canonical_specification_hash_match
  + [freshness_check] is kernel_record_schema_hash_match
  + [freshness_check] is operator_contract_hash_match
  + [freshness_check] is proof_ledger_contract_hash_match
  + [freshness_check] is generated_output_nonpromotion_policy_hash_match
  + [freshness_check] is no_live_effect_policy_hash_match
  + [freshness_check] is downstream_consumption_gate_hash_match
  + [resume_result] is resumable
  + [resume_result] is blocked_for_stale_authority
  + [resume_result] is blocked_for_missing_proof
  + [resume_result] is interrupted_for_SOP_judgment
  + [resume_result] is rebake_required

  = must: require blocked_for_stale_authority when accepted authority hashes do not match the checkpoint basis
  = must: require interrupted_for_SOP_judgment when checkpoint state is internally consistent but current meaning, authority, or repair path is ambiguous
  = must: require rebake_required when the graph contract or operator mapping changes enough that checkpoint resume would change case meaning

& [P5RuntimeProjectionAndGeneratedOutputSeparationRules] is the projection and generated-output separation rule set
  + [separated_record_class] is graph_procedure_state
  + [separated_record_class] is checkpoint_state
  + [separated_record_class] is graph_transition_trace
  + [separated_record_class] is generated_output_trace
  + [separated_record_class] is surface_projection
  + [separated_record_class] is proof_ledger
  + [separated_record_class] is SOP_source_authority
  + [separated_record_class] is canonical_specification

  = must: keep graph procedure state and checkpoint state outside generated output roots unless future implementation activation explicitly defines ignored runtime trace paths
  = must: keep generated output traces non-authoritative and consumable only through accepted proof ledgers and absence proofs
  = must: keep surface projections read-only projections of authority class and freshness state

& [P5S02DownstreamGate] is the gate opened by P5-S02
  + [opened_slice] is P5-S03 operator node mapping and deterministic transition contract
  + [activation_basis] is graph procedure state envelope and checkpoint nonauthority accepted
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is operator-to-node mapping determines which SOP duties can be mechanical and when the graph must stop for judgment
  + [completion_review_required] is true

  = must: open P5-S03 only after P5-S02 completion review accepts this graph procedure state envelope and checkpoint nonauthority contract
